# Client UI

The client is presentational. Its job is to deal cards visually, capture the user's selection, send the snap to the server, and animate the response. It is **never** the source of truth for game state.

## State boundaries

- **Server state** (decks, sessions, content catalog, profile): React Query. Cache key prefixed by feature: `['session', id]`, `['deck', deckId]`, `['content', 'cards']`.
- **Active game session** (selected card, selected PM, animation flags, ticker): `GameSessionContext` reducer. Lives only on `PlayPage` and is reset on session end.
- **Auth**: `useAuth0` from the SDK. Don't proxy it through context.
- **Forms**: `useState` is fine. Bring in `react-hook-form` only if a form has more than four fields.

## Optimistic UI

Pre-render the snap result on the client using the mirrored engine (`client/src/game/engine/`). When the server response arrives, **replace** the optimistic state with the server's authoritative state. If they disagree, the server wins. Surface a small reconciliation toast in dev only.

## Design tokens

Game-themed colors and typography come from `client/src/styles/tokens.css`. Reach for these before any Tailwind color or hex literal.

| Token | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `var(--ink)` / `var(--ink2)` | Masthead, dark sections |
| `var(--cream)` / `var(--white)` | Page bg, card bg |
| `var(--muted)` / `var(--rule)` | Labels, dividers |
| `var(--red)` / `var(--red-mid)` | Blitz FC team color |
| `var(--blue)` / `var(--blue-mid)` | Storm SC team color |
| `var(--green-field)` / `var(--green-turf)` | Field, selection states |
| `var(--gold)` | Playmaker accents, DP, status ticker |

Typography: `Playfair Display SC` for scores and team names, `Playfair Display` italic for card and section names, `Source Serif 4` italic for body. These are loaded once in `styles/fonts.css`.

## Tailwind

Use Tailwind for layout, spacing, responsive breakpoints, hover states, focus rings. Do **not** use Tailwind for game-skin colors (`bg-red-600`, `text-blue-700`) — use the design tokens.

## Components

- One component per file. PascalCase filename.
- Co-locate small subcomponents only if they're used nowhere else.
- Props interfaces named `<ComponentName>Props`.
- Avoid prop drilling beyond two levels — lift to `GameSessionContext` or React Query.

## Mobile-first

The whole game must work one-handed on a 375px viewport. Tap targets ≥ 44px. No hover-only interactions. Test resize behavior on every screen.

## Accessibility

- Every interactive element is reachable by keyboard.
- Cards have `role="button"` and `aria-pressed` for selection state.
- The status ticker has `aria-live="polite"`.
- Color is never the only signal — every selection state has a border or icon change too.

## API client

All HTTP calls go through `client/src/services/api.ts`. It's an axios instance with an interceptor that injects the Auth0 access token. Don't call `fetch` directly.

```typescript
import api from '@/services/api';

const session = await api.get(`/sessions/${id}`).then((r) => r.data);
```

## Admin pages

`/admin/*` routes are wrapped with `<RequireAdmin>` (a component that calls `useRequireAdmin` and redirects non-admins to `/`). Server-side gating in `requireAdmin` middleware is the actual security boundary; this is just UX.
